    "updated_at": "2026-06-19T08:49:23Z",
    "body": "I'm also confused by the wording in the standard. I reviewed the behavior in Chrome 149 and Firefox 152 and found they do not agree.\n\nHere's an example:\n\n(`applet`, `marquee` and `object` seem to be interchangeable tags here)\n\n[`<nobr><table><marquee></table><nobr>`](https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?%3Cnobr%3E%3Ctable%3E%3Cmarquee%3E%3C%2Ftable%3E%3Cnobr%3E)\n\nFirefox:\n\n```\n└─HTML\n  ├─HEAD\n  └─BODY\n    └─NOBR\n      ├─MARQUEE\n      ├─TABLE\n      └─NOBR\n```\n\n`NOBR` nests.\n\nChrome:\n\n```\n└─HTML\n  ├─HEAD\n  └─BODY\n    ├─NOBR\n    │ ├─MARQUEE\n    │ └─TABLE\n    └─NOBR\n```\n\n`NOBR` siblings.\n\nI also tried lexbor via [PHP's `Dom\\HTMLDocument` 8.5.7](https://3v4l.org/aO99F#v8.5.7) and got this result on serialize: `<nobr><marquee></marquee><table></table><nobr></nobr></nobr>\n`. This seems to correspond to the Firefox tree with nested `NOBR`.",
