    "updated_at": "2026-06-19T10:57:30Z",
    "body": "Good example, thank you. So Alex (lexbor author) was [wrong about this](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9559#issuecomment-1703973354), it can happen. \n\nUnfortunately, Firefox/lexbor are not authoritative here because they don't call `any_other_end_tag` at all, so their behavior is not standard. This example should be added to html5tests, so that Firefox/lexbor could fix it, but this issue is more about the difference between Ladybird and Chrome (see [the first message](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9559#issue-1821261026)).\n\nI wonder what Ladybird tree looks like. I am currently building Ladybird, but it will take more than 7 hours on my machine...",
