    "updated_at": "2026-06-19T18:36:04Z",
    "body": "Hi @sirreal @stasoid \n\n@sirreal thanks for the example; it looks like Chrome and Safari are handling it correctly.\n@stasoid It seems we do need to call `any-other-end-tag` after all. I've restored this behavior, and everything works just like it does in Chrome and Safari; all current html5lib tests are passing successfully as well.\n\nDoesn't the `Live DOM Viewer` use the current DOM from the browser in which it's open?\nThe result varies from browser to browser. Or am I wrong, and am I misunderstanding something?\n\nP.S.: @sirreal, you found a really cool test.",
